# NOTE: these patterns must stay root-anchored (leading `/`). A bare `build/`
# matches ANY directory so named, and the vendored pip contains the real source
# directory `pip/_internal/operations/build/`, which would then be silently
# excluded from the repo and break a fresh CI build with
# `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pip._internal.operations.build'`.
/build/
/.gradle/
